  "scopeReview": {
    "assignedAssertion": "AT-ops-9: foreground, child, research, and original background routes identify Sol/max/Fast, Luna/max/Fast, Sol/medium/Fast with the pinned research skill, and Sol/max/Fast; the experimental high/no-Fast arm has a separate receipt and cannot amend the original route.",
    "proposedCases": [
      "foreground-original-route",
      "ordinary-child-route",
      "research-pinned-skill",
      "background-arm-isolation"
    ],
    "assessment": [
      "Four positive cases cover the exact named assertion at its assigned CLI rung.",
      "The existing ModelRoute.select, invoke, delegationReceipt and ModelRouteProbe.run interfaces are sufficient; the plan does not require owner, API, DTO, policy, module, provider protocol or CLI command changes.",
      "The child and research cases reuse existing delegation helpers and fixed external fixtures; the research output remains synthetic and uses the pinned skill resources.",
      "The background case sequences original, experimental high/default and original routes, and refuses the experimental foreground selection. This is enough to check arm separation without adding another role/arm matrix.",
      "The nine policy and nine delegation checks in the verification section are existing regression cases, not new AT-ops-9 cases or a duplicated implementation matrix.",
      "The plan explicitly keeps wholeATComplete false and defers protected production route proof and whole AT/card/release acceptance."
    ]
  },
